Z||000000||Songman||06-09-2001||06:53 PM||||1979 Dodge Power Wagon W15 (3/4 ton) stepside for sale. <P>This truck has pulled everything in Nashville out of the mud! But now the tranny is out and I don't want to put any money into fixing it because of all of the other projects I have.<P>318 ci, automatic tranny, Chevrolet axles with Warn locking hubs.<P>Brand new Mickey Thompson claws that are worth the asking price for the truck.<P>$250 worth of new tie rods ends still in the boxes.<P>Obviously this is not a perfect truck cosmetically or it would be a lot higher price. I rated it as a 3 and looked up the retail in a specialty truck book and it listed at $3200. I figure $1000 with all the new stuff you get is plenty to make up for the tranny. Maybe it can be rebuilt, I don't know. I was just driving down the road one day and it clunked. I had it towed home and that is where it still sits.<P>This is one tough looking truck. Sits high and looks mean. I have never parked this truck without someone talking to me about it. You don't see stepsides anymore.<P>Has aluminum Edelbrock intake and chrome Edelbrock carberator.<P>No a/c. Has sliding back glass and vent windows.<P>Any questions, just ask...<P>Oh yeah... for an extra hundred I will throw in a set of Champ 500 aluminum wheels for the truck. It has chrome steel wheels on it now. The kind with the holes all around..<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 06-09-2001).]||||reg||1
